MENTOR: Here's Title at 1 s, halfway through its first move. The "An easing lesson" text is still faint because its Opacity is mid-fade.

Right now Title's Position, Scale and Opacity all run at constant speed between 0.5 s and 1.5 s. Everything starts moving at full speed at 0.5 s and stops dead at 1.5 s, which looks mechanical. Easing makes the motion slow into and out of each keyframe, the way real objects move.

To ease a pair:
1. Select the layer and press U to show its keyframes.
2. Select the two keys of a pair.
3. Choose **Animation > Keyframe Assistant > Easy Ease**, or press F9.
4. To check, open the Graph Editor. Straight lines mean linear. S-shaped curves mean eased. The keyframe icons also change from diamonds to hourglass shapes.

These are your four pairs, all on Title:
- Position, 0.5 to 1.5 s
- Position, 1.5 to 3 s
- Scale, 0.5 to 1.5 s
- Opacity, 0.5 to 1.5 s

Try easing all four yourself, then tell me "done" and I'll check. If you'd like to watch me do one first, just ask.

